class.description:
[TTSServer] speaks text with a [TTSPersona], keeps a list of named personas and emits one signal per utterance event. The speech itself is done by the platform through [DisplayServer] ([method DisplayServer.tts_speak] and the other [code]tts_*[/code] methods), which stay available as before.
If the voice of a persona does not exist on the current machine, [TTSServer] picks a voice for the persona's language instead (see [method resolve_voice_id]), so a saved persona works on every platform.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	TTSServer.utterance_ended.connect(_on_utterance_ended)

	var guard = TTSPersona.new()
	guard.persona_name = "guard"
	guard.language = "en"
	guard.pitch = 0.8
	TTSServer.add_persona(guard)

	var id = TTSServer.speak("Halt! Who goes there?", TTSServer.get_persona("guard"))
	if id == -1:
		print("Text to speech is not available.")

func _on_utterance_ended(id):
	print("Utterance %d finished." % id)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
	TtsServer.UtteranceEnded += OnUtteranceEnded;

	var guard = new TtsPersona();
	guard.PersonaName = "guard";
	guard.Language = "en";
	guard.Pitch = 0.8f;
	TtsServer.AddPersona(guard);

	long id = TtsServer.Speak("Halt! Who goes there?", TtsServer.GetPersona("guard"));
	if (id == -1)
	{
		GD.Print("Text to speech is not available.");
	}
}

private void OnUtteranceEnded(long id)
{
	GD.Print($"Utterance {id} finished.");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Text to speech must be enabled with the project setting [member ProjectSettings.audio/general/text_to_speech]. Otherwise, and with the headless display server, [method is_available] returns [code]false[/code], [method speak] reports an error and returns [code]-1[/code], and the other methods do nothing.
[b]Note:[/b] Signals are always emitted on the main thread, even if the platform reports the events from another thread. They are emitted for all utterances, also for those started directly with [method DisplayServer.tts_speak].
